# ============================================================================
# Koru .gitignore - Whitelist Approach for Root Directory
# ============================================================================
# Strategy: ignore root FILES by default, then whitelist the essential ones.
#
# READ THE NEXT SENTENCE BEFORE TRUSTING THE LINE ABOVE. `/*` does not ignore
# everything at root, because the two re-includes under it give back most of
# what it caught: `!*/` allows EVERY directory and `!.*` allows EVERY dotfile.
# So a tool that drops `.anything/` or `anything/` at the repo root is tracked
# by default, and only an explicit rule further down stops it. The header used
# to claim "ignore everything at root by default", which is the opposite of
# what happens to directories, and a 2.8 MB `.shell-probe/` of build scratch
# sat untracked-but-trackable until a ceremony commit nearly swept it in
# (2026-08-07; the ceremony now stages by name, never `-A`, 2026-08-31).

# Ignore root-level files
/*

# ...but allow directories (SEE ABOVE — this is why build dirs need naming)
!*/

# ...and allow dotfiles (SEE ABOVE — same hole, same fix)
!.*

# Globally allow Markdown files
!*.md
!**/*.md

# ============================================================================
# WHITELIST: Essential Files at Root
# ============================================================================

# Documentation
!README.md
!SPEC.md
!KORU.md
!STATUS.md
!CLAUDE.md
!CLAUDE.md.template
!DOCUMENTATION.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md

# Build configuration
!build.zig
!build.zig.zon
!koru.json

# Scripts
!run_regression.sh
!analyze_leaks.sh
!run_single_test.sh

# Node.js (tooling only - not runtime dependency)
!package.json

# Corpus curation (generator config; .md is allowed by *.md whitelist)
!koru-by-example.json

# Visual + sonic identity — the MANIFEST for the face whose matter lives in ./visual/.
# The root whitelist above had swallowed it, which quietly broke the whole convention:
# ./visual/ was tracked, so a clone got the ART, while the file DECLARING it was
# ignored — and a face nobody can read is not a face. It only ever worked locally
# because consumers were reading it out of this working tree.
!visual-identity.json

# Git files
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes

# ============================================================================
# Build Artifacts (Anywhere in Project)
# ============================================================================

# Distribution (npm package build artifacts)
dist/

.zig-cache/
zig-out/
*.o
*.hi
a.out

# koru_std build outputs
koru_std/koru_out

# Agent-harness shell scratch. Not koru's — a tool compiles into it at the repo
# root, leaving a .zig-cache and a backend.zig behind. Needs naming explicitly
# because the whitelist at the top re-includes it TWICE: `!*/` allows every
# directory and `!.*` allows every dotfile, so `/*` never catches it. It reached
# 2.8 MB before anyone looked, and the status ceremony's own instructions say
# `git add -A`.
/.shell-probe/

# Node.js dependencies (tooling only)
node_modules/

